module gunbc.whole_root_blocking_diagnostic_roster

import std.types { NonEmptyStr, Int, List }
import extdeps.external_authority { CitedFigureStanding, TranscribedUncited }

// THE STANDING BLOCKING POPULATION OF THE WHOLE-ROOT COMPILE, keyed by identity rather than counted
// (DESIGN section 5: a monotone debt contract joins at identity grain, never by count). The join
// that consumes it is not built: running the whole-root compile on a schedule or gate is a
// standing claim on a paid runner and waits on an operator ruling. That frontier and its trigger
// are declared as gunbc.rung_drop.compiler_change_refusals_land_outside_every_compiled_closure.
//
// IDENTITY IS (module, verbatim message, occurrence), NOT (module, diagnostic variant), and NOT
// line and column. The CLI prints no variant, and adding one would be seed growth
// (gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing PublicSurfaceGrowth; gunbc.emit_diagnostic_observation declines
// the same growth and decodes the rendering instead). The message is finer than a variant anyway:
// it names the offending symbol. Positions are left out because any edit above a line moves them
// (DESIGN section 3: cite the symbol, not the position). occurrence is the 1-based ordinal among
// rows sharing a module and message, so the roster is a multiset and every row has its own identity.
type WholeRootBlockingDiagnostic {
  module: NonEmptyStr
  message: NonEmptyStr
  occurrence: Int
}

// WHAT THESE ROWS ARE, stated as a typed bet (DESIGN section 4d). They were transcribed from one
// run on one revision by a hand split of the rendering, not produced by a declared classifier.
// So they are not an observation, and they are not a RepositoryCensusObservation, whose method_run
// would claim a run that never happened.
data whole_root_blocking_diagnostic_snapshot_standing: CitedFigureStanding = TranscribedUncited {
  read_obligation: "Snapshot of the 2026-09-23 state: gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --target dag --repository gunbc --measured-root-demands tools/whole_corpus_compile_measured_root_demands.json, run by session neat-ibex-861 with a binary built at a608c8c852f0bc69420e0bba1011ca8d6ce46c03 (main merged with gunbc#12143, which adds none of these rows). The run reported 500 blocking diagnostics over 5454 dag-primary sources; 1198 census-only modules were not compiled and are absent. The 280 rows under dag/gunbc/namespace/transition_admission/ are omitted because gunbc#12195 deletes those files. RE-SEED these rows, replacing rather than amending them, from the first whole-root run on the gated head decoded by gunbc.emit_diagnostic_observation read_emit_diagnostics, whose population is cross-checked against the compiler's own blocking total." as NonEmptyStr,
}

